SUMMARY:Lisa Jarrett Book Release and Artist Talk
DESCRIPTION:Lisa Jarrett joins Dr. Kiara Hill and exhibition co-curator Jaleesa Johnston in conversation about the exhibition Tenderhead and themes of migration\, family\, and care examined through the lens of Beauty Supply and Black hair rituals. The seated program takes place within the exhibition\, surrounded by Lisa’s richly layered artworks. \n\n\n\n6:30 pmConversation with the artist\, Thelma Johnson Streat Black Art & Experiences Gallery \n\n\n\n7:30 pmBook release and reception\, Fields Ballroom \n\n\n\nFollowing the discussion\, be the first to get your one-of-a-kind copy of the exhibition catalogue\, on sale at the event. 
URL:https://portlandartmuseum.org/event/lisa-jarrett-book-release-and-artist-talk/
LOCATION:Portland Art Museum\, 1219 SW Park Ave\, Portland\, OR\, 97205
CATEGORIES:Free & discounted,Lectures & talks
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://portlandartmuseum.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Reinstallation-Tenderhead_CFU_034-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
