SUMMARY:The Maker’s Table | A Winemaker Dinner Series
DESCRIPTION:Portland Art Museum Venues invites you to The Maker’s Table—an intimate evening series bringing together Oregon winemakers and visual artists for a one-of-a-kind experience of wine\, art and conversation. \n\n\n\nHeld after hours in the Museum’s stunning new Rothko Pavillion\, each evening explores the creative process behind both disciplines. Guests are invited not to simply taste and observe\, but to engage; discovering how inspiration takes shape\, how tension fuels beauty\, and how artistry evolves over time.   \n\n\n\nThis season of our Maker’s Table Series will include five unforgettable events—each featuring a different visual artist represented by the Portland Art Museum’s Rental Sales Gallery paired with an Oregon winery. \n\n\n\nGuests may choose from two experiences: the Tasting Experience (6 – 8 p.m.) or the Maker’s Table Dinner (Tasting + Dinner). \n\n\n\nTasting Experience (6 – 8 p.m.) | $135 \n\n\n\nA conversation driven\, walk-around tasting in the Rothko Pavillion’s Community Commons featuring curated wine pours\, seasonal passed appetizers\, and artwork on view throughout the space.  The experience includes a moderated conversation between the featured winemaker and visual artist.  \n\n\n\nMaker’s Table Dinner (Tasting + Dinner) | $295  \n\n\n\nBegin the evening with the Pre-Dinner Tasting followed by a three-course\, plated dinner with curated wine pairings\, and a chef-driven menu.  \n\n\n\nThis meal will take place in the Rothko Pavillion’s third floor gallery\, overlooking both the city and the museum’s magnificent Grand Gallery.  Guests will be joined by that evening’s featured winemaker and visual artist for a more intimate continuation of the conversation. \n\n\n\nThe Maker’s Table Season Lineup \n\n\n\nMay 21\, 2026 | Alexana Winery – Winemaker Tresider Burns + Visual Artist: Hazel Schlesinger (RSG Artist) \n\n\n\nJune 18\, 2026 | Big Table Farm – Winemaker Brian Marcy & Clare Carver + Visual Artist: Clare Carver (of Big Table Farm) \n\n\n\nJuly 16\, 2026 | Antica Terra– Winemaker Maggie Harrison \n\n\n\nAugust 20\, 2026 | Cristom Vineyards – Winemaker Daniel Estrin + Visual Artist: Satoko Motouji  \n\n\n\nSeptember 17\, 2026 | Soter Vineyards – Winemaker Tony Soter \n\n\n\n*Participating Visual artists to be announced in the coming months\, in partnership with Portland Art Museum’s Rental Sales Gallery. \n\n\n\nSeating is limited for each event. We encourage early booking. \n\n\n\nProceeds from The Maker’s Table series help the mission of the Portland Art Museum
URL:https://portlandartmuseum.org/event/the-makers-table-may-21/
LOCATION:Portland Art Museum\, 1219 SW Park Ave\, Portland\, OR\, 97205
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://portlandartmuseum.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/3.2026-Rothko-Insider-Event-Cristom-Wine-Bottles-scaled.png
END:VEVENT
